    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d331">

                <pb facs="0326" n="316" sameAs="frus:frus1941v05/pg316"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 P.W./560: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Japan</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Grew</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Tokyo</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1941-10-10T21:00:00+09:00">October 10, 1941—9
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received October 10—2:38 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1606. For the Secretary and the Under Secretary only. I learn from an absolutely
                    reliable source that the proposed forthcoming landing of further Japanese forces
                    in northern Indochina is for the purpose of attacking Yunnan in order to sever
                    the Burma route. This information should be most carefully guarded.<anchor n="6"
                        xml:id="d331-f1"/>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Grew</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d331-f1" n="6" xml:id="d331-f1-content">
                <p>For substance of warning of probable reaction of the United States Government to
                    such landings, see memorandum of October 9 by the Counselor of Embassy in Japan,
                        <ref target="frus1931-41v02#pg_669">
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Foreign Relations</hi>, Japan, 1931–1941, vol. <hi
                            rendition="#small-caps">ii</hi>, p. 669</ref>. The Ambassador in Japan
                    reported to the Department concerning this warning in his telegram No. 1601,
                    October 10, 3 p.m. (740.0011 P.W./559).</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
